{{Quote|Sir, the ''Electrum'' has reverted to realspace.|A technician, to [[Wilhuff Tarkin]]|<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref>}}
[[File:Starfield.jpg|thumb|right|250px|In realspace, stars, planets, and other astronomical objects existed separated by a vast vacuum]]
'''Realspace''',<ref name="Tarkin" /> also called '''normal space''',<ref name="DB hyperdrive">{{Databank|hyperdrive|Hyperdrive}}</ref> '''space-normal''' to the [[Chiss]],<ref name="Chaos Rising">''[[Thrawn Ascendancy: Chaos Rising]]''</ref> '''star-space''' to the [[Kilji]] [[species]],<ref name="Lesser Evil">''[[Thrawn Ascendancy: Lesser Evil]]''</ref> or simply '''space''',<ref name="TRB">''[[The Rebellion Begins]]''</ref> was the dimension in which all of [[the galaxy]]'s residents lived. The vast majority of space was a [[vacuum]], a depressurized volume devoid of [[atmosphere]]. The vacuum of space was fatal to many living organisms without the use of some sort of [[Environment suit|EVA suit]] and was unable to sustain [[fire]].<ref name="LotS">''[[Lords of the Sith]]''</ref> Because travel using [[sublight engine]]s within realspace was slow, [[Sentience|sentients]] found a technological way to access the shadow dimension known as [[hyperspace]]. A [[starship]] equipped with a [[hyperdrive]] would "jump" from realspace into hyperspace, and "revert" from hyperspace to realspace.<ref name="Tarkin" />

[[Species]] that could survive in the vacuum of space include [[exogorth]]s<ref name="ESB">{{Film|V}}</ref> and [[Cylo]]'s [[cyborg]] [[whale-ship]]s.<ref name="Vader 5">[[Darth Vader (2015) 5|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 5]]</ref> [[Neebray]]s could survive in [[nebula]]e, such as the [[Kaliida Nebula]].<ref name="SoM">{{TCW|Shadow of Malevolence|Shadow of ''Malevolence''}}</ref> As well as being able to survive in space, the [[purrgil]] were capable of traveling through hyperspace.<ref name="The Call">{{Rebels|The Call}}</ref>

Many [[droid]]s were able to operate in space. [[Astromech droid]]s were exposed to the vacuum of space when conducting repairs outside the hull of a starship<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> and when inserted into the astromech socket of a [[starfighter]].<ref name="RotS">{{Film|III}}</ref> [[KX-series security droid]]s could also survive in the vacuum of space.<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> Battle droids, used by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars]], occasionally sat on the outside of ships, such as pod-hunting shuttles.<ref name="Rising Malevolence Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/rising-malevolence-episode-guide|text="Rising Malevolence" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref>

